{"id":"word:hebrew:H376","type":"word","title":"אִישׁ","subtitle":"H376 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a man as an individual or a male person; often used as an adjunct to a more definite term (and in such cases frequently not expressed in translation)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אִישׁ (H376) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 2187 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אִישׁ (ʼîysh) means a man as an individual or a male person; often used as an adjunct to a more definite term (and in such cases frequently not expressed in translation) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 4 12."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אִישׁ","transliteration":"ʼîysh","pronunciation":"eesh","strong":"H376","lemmaId":"hebrew:H376","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["אִ֣ישׁ","אִ֥ישׁ","אִ֖ישׁ","אִישׁ","אִ֔ישׁ"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",909],["HNcmsc",212],["HNcmpc",169],["HTd/Ncmsa",167],["HTd/Ncmpa",121],["HNcmpa",112],["HC/Ncmsa",104],["HR/Ncmsa",83],["HRd/Ncmsa",41],["HC/Ncmsc",36]]},"definitions":{"short":"a man as an individual or a male person; often used as an adjunct to a more definite term (and in such cases frequently not expressed in translation)","usage":"also, another, any (man), a certain, champion, consent, each, every (one), fellow, (foot-, husband-) man, (good-, great, mighty) man, he, high (degree), him (that is), husband, man(-kind), none, one, people, person, steward, what (man) soever, whoso(-ever), worthy. Compare 802 .","full":"H376. ish אִישׁ 2166 noun masculine man ( = vir ) (MI, SI, Phoenician אש , perhaps also Sabean אסם compare Prät l.c , but DHM ZMG 1883, 330 ) — ׳א absolute Gen 2:23 +; construct 25:27 +; suffix אִישִׁי 29:32 +, etc.; plural אִישִׁים Psa 141:4 2 t. (Phoenician אשם ); usually אֲנָשִׁים Gen 12:20 +, from √ אנשׁ q. v.; construct אַנְשֵׁי Judg 6:27 +; suffix אֲנָשַׁי 1Sam 23:12 etc.; — man , opposed to woman Gen 2:23-24 , Lev 20:27 ; Num 5:6 ; Deut 17:2 f; Josh 6:21 ; 8:25 ; Jer 40:7 , emphasis on sexual distinction & relation Gen 19:8 ; 24:16 ; 38:25 ; Exod 22:15 ; Lev 15:16 ( זָרַ֑ע שִׁכְבַת ) 15:18 ( שׁ אֹתָהּ אִישׁ יִשְׁכַּב ׳זֿ׳אֲשֶׁר וְאִשָּׁה ) 20:10 f; Num 5:13 f; Deut 22:22 f; Isa 4:1 +; thence = husband , especially with suffix Gen 3:6 , 16 ; 16:3 ; 29:32 , 34 ; Lev 21:7 ; Num 30:7 f; Deut 28:56 ; Judg 13:8 f; Ruth 1:3 f; 1Sam 25:19 ; Jer 29:6 ; Ezek 16:45 +; figurative of ׳י as husband of Israel אִישִׁי Hosea 2:18 (opposed to בַּעְלִּי ); man as procreator, father Eccl 6:3 ; of male child Gen 4:1 compare אֲנָשִׁים זֶרַע 1Sam 1:11 ; man , opposed to beast Exod 11:7 ; Lev 20:15 (compare אָדָם ); compare figurative Psa 22:7 but also of male of animals Gen 7:2 (twice in verse) ( וְאִשְׁתּוֺ אִישׁ ); man , opposed to God 32:29 ; Num 23:19 וִיכַזֵּב אֵל אִישׁ לֹא (|| וְיִתְנֶחָ֑ם וּבֶןאָֿדָם ); Job 9:32 ; 32:13 ; Hosea 11:9 compare Isa 31:8 ; Job 12:10 ( אִישׁ כָּלבְּֿשַׂר רוּחַ ); hence in phrases to denote ordinary, customary, common אֲנָשִׁים שֵׁבֶט 2Sam 7:14 (|| אָדָם בְּנֵי נִגְעֵי ); אֲנָשִׁים לֶחֶם Ezek 24:17 , 22 [** אֲנָשִׁים 24:17 ; 24:22 is textual error; We (apparently Sm) אֲנֻשִׁים ; Toy Hpt אוֺנִים ( Hosea 9:4 ).] (compare Isa 8:1 ); אַמַּתאִֿישׁ Deut 3:11 ; but also contracted אָדָם Psa 49:3 ; 62:10 ; man , as valiant 1Sam 4:9 (twice in verse) ( לַאֲנָשִׁים וִהְיוּ ) so 1Kin 2:2 compare 1Sam 26:15 ; so חַיִל אִישׁ 31:12 ; 2Sam 24:9 ; 1Kin 1:42 +; also מִלְחָמָה אִישׁ Num 31:49 ; Deut 2:14 , 16 ; Josh 5:4 , 6 +; even of ׳י Exod 15:3 מִלְחָמָה אִישׁ יהוה ; often prefixed to other nouns in apposition ׳א אָדוֺן Gen 42:30 , 33 , ׳א וְשֹׁפֵט שַׂר Exod 2:14 , ׳א כֹּהֵן Lev 21:9 , ׳א סָרִיס Jer 38:7 ; particular before adjective, of a people מִצְרִי אִישׁ Gen 39:1 ; Exod 2:11 , 19 compare Gen 37:28 ; 38:1-2 , 39:14 ; 1Sam 17:12 ; 30:11 , 13 +; a man as resident in, or belonging to a place or people Num 25:6 ; Judg 10:1 + (so Phoenician); usually plural יִשְׂרָאֵל אַנְשֵׁי 1Sam 7:11 ; 31:7 (twice in verse) compare Josh 7:4-5 , +; also singularcollective Deut 27:14 ; Josh 9:6-7 , Judg 20:11 ; 1Sam 11:8 (see Dr) +; 2Sam 10:6 , 8 ( ׳א טוֺב ); (so MI 10 ; MI 13 ); men = retainers, followers, soldiers 1Sam 18:27 ; 23:3 ; f 24:3 ; 25:13 +? Deut 33:8 singular collective see Di; אֱלֹהִים אִישׁ man of God = prophet 33:1 ; Josh 14:6 ; 1Sam 9:6 f; 1Kin 12:13 f + (see אלהים ); in phrase followed by abstract ׳א מִלְחָמָה חַיִל, אִישׁ see above; ׳א שֵׂיבָה Deut 32:25 , ׳א הַדָּמִים 2Sam 16:7 compare see 8, ׳א הַבְּלִיַּעַל 16:7 , ׳א מָוֶת 1Kin 2:26 , ׳א חָמָס Psa 140:12 ; Prov 3:31 +; followed by word of occupation, etc. שָׂדֶה׳א Gen 25:27 , הָאֲדָמָה׳א 9:20 (compare Zech 13:5 ), הַבֵּנַיִם ׳א champion 1Sam 17:4 (compare Dr) 17:23 , ׳א בְּשׂרָה 2Sam 18:20 , עֲצָתוֺ אִישׁ his counsellor Isa 40:13 , compare חֶרְמִי אִישׁ 1Kin 20:42 , ׳א רֵעִים Prov 18:24 ; often distributive = each, every Gen 9:5 ; 10:5 ; 40:5 (twice in verse); Exod 12:3 +; including women Job 42:11 ; 1Chr 16:3 כִּכַּרלֶֿחֶם לְאִישׁ אִשָּׁה וְעַד מֵאִישׁ יִשְׂרָאֵל לְכָלאִֿישׁ וַיְחַלֵּק ; of inanimate things 1Kin 7:30 , 36 ; also אִישׁ אִישׁ Exod 36:4 ; Num 4:19 , 49 ; Ezek 14:4 , 7 +; any one Exod 34:3 (twice in verse); 34:24 +; also אִישׁ אִישׁ Lev 15:2 ; 22:4 , 18 +; of gods 2Kin 18:33 = Isa 36:18 ; one...another אֶתקְֿרֹבוֺ וְאִישׁ אֶתרֵֿעֵהוּ וְאִישׁ אֶתאָֿחִיו אִישֿׁ וְהִרְגוּ Exod 32:27 , אָחִיו ֗֗֗ אִישׁ Deut 1:16 ; Micah 7:2 (see אָח ), אִישׁרֵ֗֗֗עֵהוּ Gen 11:3 , 7 + (see רֵעַ ) of inanimate things 15:10 .","rootNote":"contracted for 582 (or perhaps rather from an unused root meaning to be extant );","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 4 12","keyReferences":["1Chr 4 12","1Chr 4 22","1Chr 4 42","1Chr 5 18","1Chr 5 24","1Chr 5 24","1Chr 7 21","1Chr 7 40"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":2187,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 4 12","book":"1Chr","chapter":4,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWo